HTML_LEGEND='<details class="pgtk-legend" open><summary><strong>Interpretation and visual legend</strong></summary><ul><li>Plot colors distinguish categories unless explicitly defined otherwise; color intensity is not confidence.</li><li>IGV bases: A green, C blue, G orange, T red. Colored bases are reference mismatches, not automatically event support.</li><li>Grey read bodies are ordinary alignments. Whole-read colors describe alignment properties, not ALT support.</li><li>Insertion markers denote inserted sequence. Black marks can represent deletions, skipped regions, pair connectors, or downsampling depending on placement.</li><li>event_display shows overlapping reads; exact_alt_display exact ALT reads; reference_display clean REF reads.</li><li>RNA splice-junction CIGAR N operations are expected and do not invalidate exact allele evidence.</li><li>Predicted impact and consequence describe the candidate allele, not read validation. NO_EXACT_ALT_SUPPORT means no qualifying alignment contained the exact normalized ALT. RNA observations are not automatically DNA-confirmed somatic variants.</li></ul></details>'
MARKDOWN_LEGEND='\n## Interpretation and visual legend\n\n- Plot colors distinguish categories unless explicitly defined otherwise; color intensity is not confidence.\n- IGV bases: A green, C blue, G orange, T red. Colored bases are reference mismatches, not automatically event support.\n- Grey read bodies are ordinary alignments. Whole-read colors describe alignment properties, not ALT support.\n- Insertion markers denote inserted sequence. Black marks can represent deletions, skipped regions, pair connectors, or downsampling.\n- event_display shows overlapping reads; exact_alt_display exact ALT reads; reference_display clean REF reads.\n- RNA splice-junction CIGAR N operations are expected and do not invalidate exact allele evidence.\n- Predicted impact and consequence describe the candidate allele, not read validation. NO_EXACT_ALT_SUPPORT means no qualifying alignment contained the exact normalized ALT. RNA observations are not automatically DNA-confirmed somatic variants.\n'
